      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at $(- \\frac{7}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ and has a radius of $\\frac{3}{2},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n(x-(- \\frac{7}{2}))^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}={\\frac{3}{2}}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,(x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}=\\frac{9}{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2}+(y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((x+\\frac{7}{2})^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y-\\frac{1}{2})^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+\\frac{7}{2})+2(y-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y-\\frac{1}{2})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2(x+\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+\\frac{7}{2}}{y-\\frac{1}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
